								</p>
								<div class="newsBody">
									<p>Inverse Logic has a new website and new forums! Please visit us at <a href="http://inverselogic-mr.com">http://inverselogic-mr.com</a> and register so you can stop by and say Hello!!<br /><br /><font face="Verdana" size="2">Here are instructions on how to register and/or get forum access:<br /><br /></font><font face="Verdana"><font size="2"><strong>Register to the website<!--EZCODE BOLD END--><br /></strong>You must register to the site. To register, go here: <a href="http://inverselogic-mr.com/modules.php?name=Your_Account&amp;op=new_user">http://inverselogic-mr.com/modules.php?name=Your_Account&amp;op=new_user</a></font></font><!--EZCODE AUTOLINK END--><br /><br /><font face="Verdana" size="2">Once you have registered you will be sent a confirmation email. You must go to the link in the email, HOWEVER, you cant click it, you must copy/paste the entire link into the address bar and go there that way. This will complete the registration. Then you are registered to the site. If you go to the "Menu" panel on the left of the site there is a link to the "Members List" - this is a list of all registered users of the site and you can go there to find someones user name to Private Message them, etc.<br /><br /><!--EZCODE UNDERLINE START--><span style="TEXT-DECORATION: underline">If you are having technical difficulties with the confirmation email</span><!--EZCODE UNDERLINE END--><br />If you receive an email that has no link, or has just a bunch of symbols mixed with text... copy and paste THAT into the address bar and put the "http"and the "www" stuff in front of it and try THAT as the link. Some email programs dont recognize it for some reason.</font><br /><br /><font face="Verdana"><font size="2"><strong>HOW TO GET ACCESS TO FORUMS<!--EZCODE BOLD END--><br /></strong>To get to the new forums, there is a link to "Forums" on the "Menu" panel. The URL is: </font></font><a href="http://inverselogic-mr.com/modules.php?name=Forums"><font face="Verdana" size="2">http://inverselogic-mr.com/modules.php?name=Forums</font></a><font face="Verdana" size="2">&nbsp;.<br /><br />Once you click into the Forums there is a horizontal menu bar across the top. Click the "User Groups" button. Choose a user group that applies to you from the drop-down button (Officers are in the Officers User group, Members are in the Members User group, Probies the Probie user group, etc). Then click the button to the right "View Information". Then click the button that says "Join this Group". It will notify me that you have requested to join this group and I will add you, and then you will have access.<br /><br /></font><font face="Verdana"><font size="2"><strong>DKP Page<!--EZCODE BOLD END--><br /></strong>The DKP page is accessed by scrolling down the left side to the "Main Menu" panel and clicking on "DKP". The URL is: <!--EZCODE AUTOLINK START--></font></font><a href="http://inverselogic-mr.com/DKP/viewnews.php"><font face="Verdana" size="2">inverselogic-mr.com/DKP/viewnews.php</font></a><!--EZCODE AUTOLINK END--><br /><br /><font face="Verdana" size="2">You must register for this site also! Click the "Register" link. Once you are able to login, click "Standings" to see the overall DKP page. From there you can sort standings by the various categories listed there. If you do not see your name, scroll all the way to the bottom and look to the right and find the "show all" link. Click it and all names should come up.</font><br /><br /><br />If you have any questions about the website, forums, DKP page access and/or registration, please let me know.<br /><br /><br />--Aandara<br /><!--EZCODE AUTOLINK START--></p>
